or","scalar_value_finite_cutoff_antecedent","scalar_value_implementation","scalar_value_type","scope_281","support-r2-13-finite-density-call","support_backward_source","support_certificate_lean_source","support_certificate_source","support_closure_lean_source","support_closure_source","support_coercivity_source","support_contact_lean_source","support_contact_source","support_curvature_source","support_diffusion_source","support_fixed_time_polynomials","support_fixed_time_source","support_flux_source","support_forward_source","support_gap_lean_source","support_model_lean_source","support_model_source","support_optimality_chen","support_optimality_chl","support_regularity_source","support_stieltjes_lean_source","support_tails_source","support_terminal_defect_lean_source","support_terminal_lean_source","support_terminal_source","support_transfer_source","support_uniqueness_lean_source","support_variation_source"],"missing_effective_citation_ids":[]},"passage_citation_audits":[{"anchor":"gaussian-sanity-check","effective_required_citation_ids":["authored_r8_support_zero_candidate_descent","full_support_chord_derivative","scalar-r2-26-cite-paper-admissible","support_diffusion_source","support_model_lean_source","support_model_source","support_optimality_chl","support_regularity_source","support_uniqueness_lean_source","support_variation_source"],"missing_effective_citation_ids":[]}],"citation_audit_scope":"Recorded documentary references only; missing effective citation IDs do not establish a mathematical or editorial verdict.","heading_syntax":"ATX headings only; Setext and HTML headings are not parsed","scope":"Mapped passages are correspondences, not sentence-level formal support. Section-passage overlaps are document structure, not claim or proof implications. Unmapped text and passages omitted by the selector remain in the validated paper. Graph records outside the selected prerequisite closure remain in the bundle and are not asserted absent. Argument links combine recorded Lean references, curated support, formalization correspondence and explicit assumptions; their SCCs describe only that mixed recorded reachability. Reading order and platform decomposition are separate."}},"passages":[{"ref":"sha256:c4249feffa26e48c24c5690f73e0de4886e40504c8c5c0e6dcb22ec94ea334da/papers/long.md/sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/passages/gaussian-sanity-check","anchor":"gaussian-sanity-check","selected":true,"text":"\n\n<a id=\"zero-coefficient-example\"></a>\n\n### 10.3 The zero coefficient\n\nThe admissible coefficient $\\gamma_0=0$ makes the use of minimality in\nthe normalization step explicit. Its diffusion is $X_t=B_t$, and the\n[zero-coefficient heat formula][fs-reg] gives\n\n$$\nu_0(t,x)=2F_{\\mathrm G}\\!\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-t}}\\right)-1,\n\\qquad\na_0(t,x)=\\sqrt{\\frac2\\pi}\\frac{e^{-x^2/(2(1-t))}}{\\sqrt{1-t}}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbb E e^{-\\lambda B_t^2}=(1+2\\lambda t)^{-1/2}$,\n\n$$\n\\mathbb E a_0(t,B_t)=\\sqrt{\\frac2\\pi},\\qquad\n\\mathbb E a_0(t,B_t)^2=\\frac2{\\pi\\sqrt{1-t^2}},\\qquad\nq_0(t)=\\frac2\\pi\\arcsin t.\n$$\n\nThe last identity follows by integrating $q_0'=\\mathbb E a_0^2$\nfrom $q_0(0)=0$. This heat and late-step variation argument is the\nzero-field specialization of [Chen, Handschy and Lerman, Theorem 6\nand its proof, arXiv:1609.04368v4, pp. 13–16](https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.04368v4).\nStrict convexity of $\\arcsin$ gives $q_0(t)<t$\nfor $0<t<1$. Thus $G_0(s)=\\int_s^1(q_0(t)-t)\\,dt<0$ for\nevery $s<1$. Inserting an atom at $s$ is admissible, and its\n[first variation][fs-var] is $G_0(s)/2<0$. In particular, the derivative for inserting\nmass at zero is $1/4-1/\\pi<0$. Hence this coefficient does not\nminimize.\n\nHere the Euler scheme is exact: $Y_j=B_{t_j}$ under the Brownian\ncoupling. Nevertheless its normalizers are\n\n$$\nc_j=\\sqrt{\\frac\\pi2}\\,(1-t_{j-1}^2)^{1/4},\n$$\n\nso they approximate this nonconstant function of time, rather than\nconverging uniformly to one. Already $c_1=\\sqrt{\\pi/2}$ for every\nmesh. The directions $g_j$ remain orthonormal by construction and the\nrounding still preserves conditional means; the missing input to the\nvalue limit is the minimizing identity $\\mathbb E a(t,X_t)^2=1$.\n\nThe terminal spin also survives:\n$U_1=\\operatorname{sgn}(B_1)$ almost surely. But its correlation is\n\n$$\n\\mathbb E[U_1B_1]=\\sqrt{\\frac2\\pi}=\\mathcal P(\\gamma_0),\n$$\n\nthe value of this nonminimizing candidate. The negative first variation\nproves that this value is strictly above $P_*$. Admissibility, exact\nEuler sampling, and a spin-valued terminal martingale therefore do not\nsupply the minimizing normalization or identify the ground-state value.\n","content_span":{"start_byte":192326,"end_byte":194473,"start_line":4117,"end_line":4175},"block_span":{"start_byte":192288,"end_byte":194512,"start_line":4117,"end_line":4176},"section_ref":"sha256:c4249feffa26e48c24c5690f73e0de4886e40504c8c5c0e6dcb22ec94ea334da/papers/long.md/sections/178223","evidence_class":"example","rationale":"Maps this passage to Gradient martingale and the derivative of its second moment. The source locations and local guards are retained in these graph records. Exact heat-profile sanity check and nonminimiser witness; no claim that the minimiser-conditioned limit follows for this candidate.","claim_ids":["support.moment_identity","support.zero_candidate_descent"],"citation_ids":["authored_r8_support_zero_candidate_descent","full_support_chord_derivative","scalar-r2-26-cite-paper-admissible","support_diffusion_source","support_model_lean_source","support_model_source","support_optimality_chl","support_regularity_source","support_uniqueness_lean_source","support_variation_source"],"assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_admissible"]}],"correspondence_links":[{"from":"sha256:c4249feffa26e48c24c5690f73e0de4886e40504c8c5c0e6dcb22ec94ea334da/papers/long.md/sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829